                <pb facs="0555" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4114: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-02T21:00:00-05:00">October 2, 1933—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>333. Batista has just sent me word that he has placed a guard around the National
                    Hotel to prevent any further looting by soldiers and especially distribution of
                    contents of wine cellars. He assures me that the lives of all the officers now
                    in custody will be personally guaranteed by himself and that I may feel
                    confident that order will be maintained in the city tonight.</p>
                <p>From all information I can obtain, in view of the difficulty of communications,
                    all sections of the city have been relatively quiet during the past 2 hours.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
